{{ 'ness-faq.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- liquid
  assign faqs = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'question'
  assign heading_id = 'ness-faq-heading-' | append: section.id
  assign group_name = 'ness-faq-' | append: section.id
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  id="faq" is a fixed anchor, not a setting — the header, footer and hero all
  scroll here by that name, and letting it be edited would break them silently.
  scroll-margin-top (in the stylesheet) clears the floating header.

  The section element and its id render UNCONDITIONALLY, outside the "are there
  any questions" guard. Questions are the FAQ's editable surface, so an owner
  can legitimately delete the last one — and when the id lived inside the guard
  that turned every FAQ link in the theme into a silent no-op: ness-motion.js
  finds no element, returns before preventDefault, and the browser declines to
  scroll to a fragment that matches nothing. No error, no movement, nothing.
{%- endcomment -%}
<section class="ness-faq" id="faq" {% if faqs.size > 0 %}aria-labelledby="{{ heading_id }}"{% endif %}>
{%- if faqs.size > 0 -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Eyebrow, heading and rule are one centred group. All three are fixed
      copy, not settings: the FAQ's editable surface is the questions and
      answers (PLAN.md, Editability policy). The rule is decoration and carries
      no meaning, so it is hidden from assistive tech rather than announced as
      an empty element.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="ness-faq__intro" data-reveal="0">
      <p class="ness-faq__eyebrow">Good to know</p>
      <h2 class="ness-faq__heading" id="{{ heading_id }}">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <span class="ness-faq__rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </div>

    <div class="ness-faq__list">
      {%- for block in faqs -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Native <details>, so the accordion opens and closes with no
          JavaScript at all — and keeps working if a script ever fails.

          The shared `name` makes it exclusive: opening one answer closes the
          previous one, which is the prototype's behaviour (it tracks a single
          `faqOpen` index). Browsers without `name` support simply allow more
          than one open at a time, which degrades cleanly. The name carries the
          section id because a section can legally be rendered twice on a page.

          The <h3> inside <summary> is explicitly allowed by the HTML content
          model and is what gives screen-reader users a real heading list to
          navigate; it is styled back down to the design's plain question row.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          In the theme editor the exclusive `name` is dropped and the selected
          block is forced open. Otherwise selecting a question scrolls to a
          collapsed row and the merchant edits an answer they cannot see —
          and a blanket `open` with `name` still present would collapse every
          row back down to one.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <details
          class="ness-faq__item"
          {% unless request.design_mode %}name="{{ group_name }}"{% endunless %}
          {% if request.design_mode and block.selected %}open{% endif %}
          {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
        >
          <summary class="ness-faq__summary">
            <h3 class="ness-faq__question">{{ block.settings.question | escape }}</h3>
            <svg
              class="ness-faq__chevron"
              width="24"
              height="13"
              viewBox="0 0 24 13"
              fill="currentColor"
              aria-hidden="true"
              focusable="false"
            >
              <path d="M 0.319 0.317 C 0.746 -0.106 1.436 -0.106 1.862 0.317 L 12 10.385 L 22.138 0.317 C 22.564 -0.106 23.254 -0.106 23.681 0.317 C 24.106 0.74 24.106 1.426 23.681 1.849 L 12.771 12.683 C 12.345 13.106 11.655 13.106 11.229 12.683 L 0.319 1.849 C -0.106 1.426 -0.106 0.74 0.319 0.317 Z"/>
            </svg>
          </summary>

          <div class="ness-faq__answer">{{ block.settings.answer }}</div>
        </details>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
{%- endif -%}
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "FAQ",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The heading, the accordion behaviour, and all typography are fixed by the design. You can edit each question and answer, add or remove entries up to ten."
    }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 10,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "question",
      "name": "Question",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "question",
          "label": "Question",
          "default": "What is the processing time for Pre-Orders wigs?",
          "info": "Keep it to one line where possible — it sits beside the open/close arrow."
        },
        {
          "type": "richtext",
          "id": "answer",
          "label": "Answer",
          "default": "<p>Pre-order units are built to order. Construction takes 7–10 business days before the unit ships, and you will get a tracking email the moment it leaves the studio.</p>",
          "info": "One to three sentences reads best. Bold, italics, links, and lists are available."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "default": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "type": "question",
        "settings": {
          "question": "What is the processing time for Pre-Orders wigs?",
          "answer": "<p>Pre-order units are built to order. Construction takes 7–10 business days before the unit ships, and you will get a tracking email the moment it leaves the studio.</p>"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "question",
        "settings": {
          "question": "What is our return policy?",
          "answer": "<p>Because every unit is a hygiene-sensitive custom product, all sales are final. If your order arrives damaged or incorrect, email info@nessclusive.com within 48 hours of delivery and we will make it right.</p>"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "question",
        "settings": {
          "question": "Are your wigs suitable for daily wear?",
          "answer": "<p>Yes. Every unit is built on a breathable cap with a bleached, pre-plucked hairline so it can be worn daily and restyled with heat.</p>"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "question",
        "settings": {
          "question": "What is your shipping cost?",
          "answer": "<p>Shipping is calculated at checkout from your address. Nessclusive ships globally, and express options are offered at the payment step.</p>"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "question",
        "settings": {
          "question": "How do I care for my wig?",
          "answer": "<p>Wash every 8–10 wears with a sulphate-free shampoo, air dry on a mannequin head, and store on a stand away from direct sun.</p>"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "question",
        "settings": {
          "question": "When will my order get shipped?",
          "answer": "<p>Ready to Ship units leave the studio within 1–2 business days. Pre-order units ship once construction is complete.</p>"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "question",
        "settings": {
          "question": "How do I know my wig size?",
          "answer": "<p>Measure the circumference of your head at the hairline. Small is 20–21\", Medium 21.5–22.5\", Large 23\"+. Choose your cap size at checkout.</p>"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "question",
        "settings": {
          "question": "How can I check the status of my order?",
          "answer": "<p>Every order gets a confirmation and a tracking link by email. You can also text 917-587-8962 with your order number.</p>"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "question",
        "settings": {
          "question": "Can I wear a wig if I have a full head of hair?",
          "answer": "<p>Yes. Braid or cornrow your hair flat and use a wig cap underneath so the unit sits smoothly.</p>"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "question",
        "settings": {
          "question": "Can I rush my order?",
          "answer": "<p>Rush construction may be available depending on the studio calendar. Text 917-587-8962 before ordering to confirm.</p>"
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
{% endschema %}
